WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.440
Ten years ago, somewhere in Tokyo.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.330
All right, let's begin.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.000
What should I do?

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.790
Just sing, like you always do.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.760
I absolutely love your singing, Setsuna.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.470
The containment shields have been deployed.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.220
Now, let me hear you sing.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:50.070
The light shines through the feather in my grasp

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.440
Wow...

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.110
The very moment she began singing,

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:56.410
As if it was merrily dancing

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:56.200
her brain wave's electromagnetic resonance jumped by a whole twelve digits!

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:02.000
I'd like our paths to cross

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.330
As we head towards warmth and kindness

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.500
High-density libido readings are materializing.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.290
Activating Orgone charger.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:13.260
Let's begin our journey

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:18.300
This is the energy of the future!

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.970
Magnificent.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:34.780
All the laughter, all the tears—everything happened just to meet you

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.450
Always go

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.870
On my own

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.080
Always go

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:53.710
The wind blows my overflowing tears away (the wind blows them away)

00:01:53.920 --> 00:02:01.100
I try to reach out my hand time after time toward what's to come

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:07.190
I've been hurt before by careless words

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:16.110
It's time I move forward with that unchangeable past

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.660
All the laughter, all the tears—

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:29.290
everything that has happened brought me to you

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:35.340
All we have left is the future

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:41.760
Please become our reason to continue living

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:48.480
And then the sun will once again shine on us

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.330
Good morning, Lappa.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.450
Good morning, Setsuna.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.370
Good morning, Miss Mao.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.840
The hibiscus is blooming beautifully.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.710
It's colored so brilliantly.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.220
I'm happy.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:25.180
Through the
Window of Setsuna

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.560
Huh? Where's the Vice Commander?

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.190
Said she had something to take care of.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.650
Daichi...

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:43.610
Now that you're the Captain, you need to stop relying on Rita so much.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.740
You're right.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.540
It was my fault that the enemy escaped last time.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:50.830
I'm really sorry.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.540
You're the one who got us out of that mess.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:59.920
Everybody had told me that the Nebula Engine hadn't cleared its preliminary testing phase yet.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:01.800
You surprised me.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.550
It was pretty much the same thing that happened with the Earth Engine...

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:10.100
But if this'll make you feel better, I'll take it, Captain.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.690
Two more to go...

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.150
Let's do this!

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:18.820
One of them is Lady Seiren, huh?

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.110
"Lady"?

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.740
But I don't know their avatar name.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.030
What does Pitz say?

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:29.540
The image isn't as clear as last time...

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:33.500
But he says he can sense Orgone energy moving.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.460
What's Rita doing?

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:39.550
Maybe she went to get some better food...?

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.210
What?!

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:42.970
That may be possible...

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.340
No, I don't think that's it...

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.270
You were the one on the phone?

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:55.940
Yes.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.650
Thank you.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.070
I'd guessed you might be attractive from the sound of your voice,

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.160
but you're even prettier than I'd imagined.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.910
It's still early, but can I get you something to drink?

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.920
A bourbon on the rocks, then.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.380
So? What do you want to know?

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.590
You used to be a police detective.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.850
Until you quit ten years ago.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.770
Would you be willing to tell me why?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.190
Women like you scare me.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:43.280
If they think they have a good reason, they can tell any lie with a straight face.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.570
Between being a detective and a bartender,

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:51.870
I've gotten pretty good at guessing what people do for a living.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.450
A journalist, huh?

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:56.910
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:00.330
Basically, you're interested in the Kanda incident, aren't you?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:01.340
That's right.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:05.630
Yes, I was on the task force for it.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.930
But the official story is that the case was solved.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.390
What do you want to know?

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.600
Everything you know.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.390
Everything you remember.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:20.060
I don't know anything more than what was reported.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:24.780
In that case, I'd just like to hear your thoughts about the incident.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.990
That's a very delicate way of phrasing it.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.820
At the time, Macbeth Enterprises

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:36.250
was in the midst of developing a man-machine interface for mobile weaponry.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.290
Part of their research

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:43.210
culminated in the creation of six children through illegal genetic manipulation.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:50.930
An anonymous whistleblower reported this to the police,

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.970
and Macbeth was subsequently investigated.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:57.600
The police found those six children and took them into custody.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.440
Children born in Japan,

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.860
but without any kind of government records...

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:08.280
Macbeth was using those children to develop weapons.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.450
This was, of course, considered to be a major human rights violation,

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.330
and the parties believed to be responsible were arrested.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:18.080
At the same time, the Tokyo suburbs

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.710
were plagued by a string of inexplicable coma cases—

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.420
seemingly random people would fall unconscious for several days at a time.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:27.420
Macbeth's experiments were said to have caused that, as well.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.050
A short while later, Macbeth's executive cabinet was subjected to a purge,

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:38.720
and the majority of their operations were supposedly reformed.

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:41.600
Naturally,

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:46.570
members of the Kube family—the company's original founders—were the next executives.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:50.650
Kube did their best to take advantage of the incident, and returned to power.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:55.120
In the end, the whole thing was blamed on Kanda Takashi,

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:58.620
Macbeth's CEO at the time of the incident.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.580
And then...

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.000
Kanda committed suicide.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:13.300
Why did you quit the force?

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:19.270
What happened to those six children?

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.230
I see...

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:26.190
So that's what you really wanted to know.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.700
Hey, Akari... Is it okay for us to be having fun right now?

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.160
The Midsummer's Knights' motto

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.780
is "Do what you have to, when you have to."

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.490
We're free the rest of the time.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.660
Did Daichi decide that?

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.210
No, I did.

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:48.790
Aren't you going to swim after coming all the way here?

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.760
Only children go to the pool to swim.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.510
Then what did you come here to do?

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:58.970
Just relax, and enjoy all the guys looking at you.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:08:59.930
Wow.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.970
I'm jealous of the squirrel.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.060
Maybe it was a bad idea to bring Hana.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:08.900
Hey, Akari...

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.030
She's been swimming this whole time.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.110
I do wonder what really happened to them.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.450
Were there any photos?

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:22.660
No, I heard all our materials on them were destroyed.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:27.830
I was on the task force,

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:31.050
and even I don't know where they went afterward.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.550
All we were told was that

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:38.720
in order to protect their rights, measures were taken to keep their personal information confidential.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:43.020
So I of course looked into it myself,

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.310
and when they found out, I was forced to resign.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.020
Why did you look into it?

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.980
Something wasn't right.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:51.650
Wasn't right?

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:55.530
Were all of those documents really destroyed for their safety?

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.070
I didn't have any proof,

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:00.490
but it just didn't seem that way to me.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.790
What's happening?

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.040
What's going on?

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.080
What happened to them after that?

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:12.920
Unfortunately, I don't know.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.510
You'll have to ask the guys who fired me.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:19.800
Thank you.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.100
And thanks for the drink.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:26.020
Do you know where they went?

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:32.570
As you said, the government had no records on them,

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.690
but they had names inside the company.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:39.240
And they had numbers, too.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:46.000
Each of them had a serial number between three and eight.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:52.130
Which means there was also a one and two.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.130
And maybe more.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:11:00.720
Are they still involved with that illegal weapons development project?

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.260
Sometimes, I can't help but think they must be.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.770
Kanda Takashi committed suicide,

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.520
so I inherited this company and you.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:23.820
This is Kube, right?

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.160
Kanda, right?

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.960
I've been set up.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.000
But not by you.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.460
Be careful.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:39.260
I think that our meeting was

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:43.640
a very fortunate event for both parties.

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.890
You "think," eh?

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:51.270
Pac, could you kill someone?

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:55.110
Or do you ever think you want to kill someone?

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.070
There is a high probability

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:01.780
that the weapons I devise will be used to take lives on the battlefield.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:06.950
In that sense, I am indeed complicit in murder.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:12.330
But I have never thought about killing a specific individual,

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.750
nor would I do such a thing.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.550
Kanda Takashi has committed suicide.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:35.480
My sole reason for existence is the completion of my assignment.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.520
Pac does not lie.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.620
I'm out.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.370
And we're running out of capsules, too.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.250
This is bad.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:55.540
If Lady Seiren awakens, we'll be fine.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:59.040
We can make new capsules.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:03.510
Is the seat next to you free?

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.380
Sure.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:06.890
Thanks.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.230
Want some?

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:19.060
Oh, my.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:23.150
How kind of you to offer something to a complete stranger! Thank you.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:24.570
You were swimming a lot, weren't you?

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:28.780
My goal is 1,200 meters a day.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.410
Are you on a swim team or something?

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:34.000
No, I'm not.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:39.670
But I've been told to exercise so that I stay healthy.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.630
Well, that's a good thing, yeah...

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:43.920
Yes.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:47.470
I'm glad they gave me such kind advice.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.260
I could never do that.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.390
Two squirrels?

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:56.770
Did you make a friend, Pitz?

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:01.610
Lappa is my friend.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:02.610
Hey...

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.320
Does that squirrel talk?

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:09.780
Squirrels don't talk.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.950
Right?

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:16.910
How can I be the heroine, when I'm the only one without a squirrel?!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.370
This whole thing is squirrely!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:23.340
The project is finally nearing its final stages.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.840
The device we're installing

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:30.180
seems to be a system designed to give the subject a specific dream.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.930
Why does it come in pairs?

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.310
Sorry, Ban.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:39.850
I'll take care of the rest myself.
You can go home for today.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:44.400
My contract with my sponsor means

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.860
that I can't show anyone the tests, even you.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:50.280
Sorry, did that upset you?

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:58.160
No, I'm your assistant. I will, of course, do whatever you say.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:14:59.500
But...

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.920
Are you sure you can do it all on your own?

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.380
You're right.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:10.880
Wouldn't it be convenient if there were another one of me?

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.940
Eyecatch

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:19.730
I'm back.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.690
Welcome back, Setsuna.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.190
I'm so glad.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.610
It's still blooming beautifully.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.700
Isn't that nice?

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:36.830
But it seems to me that you like sitting by the window more than you like the plant.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.620
Am I right?

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.870
You're amazing, Miss Mao!

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.080
You know everything!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:49.090
A long time ago, I wasn't allowed to go outside.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:53.090
I can do that now, so I'm really happy!

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:57.810
Now that I can visit it whenever I want, the world I see outside the window

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:02.190
looks totally different than it used to.
It makes me happy to see it!

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:04.190
Okay, Setsuna.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.980
It's time for your medical checkup.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:15.030
I'm not sick, so why do you give me so many examinations?

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:19.750
Because you're very important to me.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.420
So, please take a seat in that machine.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.920
A medical equipment manufacturer?

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:30.050
Akari did some research,

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:34.470
and learned that this research group is connected to Macbeth Enterprises.

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:37.470
Then there's probably something here.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:46.900
Well, well...

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:47.900
Good to see both of you.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:49.900
You, too.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:07.000
Amarok and Malkin...

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.500
We can assume they're the enemy leaders, right?

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.210
I think so.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:16.640
But since they have avatar bodies,

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:19.850
they must have thought of themselves as Earthlings

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:22.220
until they awakened as Planetary Gears.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.100
When did they awaken?

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:32.190
If you kiss, you can read someone's mind for a second, can't you?

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:38.870
I think we have special powers because we're Designer's Children.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.540
Is that why they keep us locked up?

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.960
And why we can only see the outside world from the window?

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.340
Amara... Moco.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:51.800
Good news.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:54.210
You get to leave this place.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:56.380
You're going to a country called Japan.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:59.140
Japan?

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.100
What is this device?

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.980
This is your machine.

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:10.900
It's a Neural Maneuver System created specifically for you.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:13.190
Try it.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:42.510
You think one of their friends is here?

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:45.180
Probably. They probably haven't awakened, though.

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:48.600
You said that touching a powerful Orgone energy

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:52.690
or kissing an awakened avatar brings back their memories, right?

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:54.360
Yeah.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.780
And even if an avatar hasn't awakened,

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:01.320
if they kiss you, they can read your mind or telepathically communicate.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.340
My beautiful Setsuna...

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.340
You're so beautiful.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.600
I wonder if the Designer's Children

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:29.810
weren't actually created as pilots for new weapons,

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:34.940
but as vessels to install a human consciousness.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:40.820
In other words, if you could keep installing your mind into a young body,

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:43.030
you could become immortal.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.120
No!

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:54.880
What?

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.170
What did you see?

00:19:56.670 --> 00:20:00.670
You were raising me to be your own vessel!

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.130
You're a terrible person!

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.510
Wait, Setsuna!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:05.930
Wait!

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.130
Captain, behind you!

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:38.630
Manatsu Daichi!

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:42.470
You drove Albion mad, so you die first!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.480
This light...

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:57.900
Teppei?

00:20:58.320 --> 00:20:59.730
The Livlaster?

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:06.030
Albion was the other Neoteny that Liban was talking about?

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:14.500
Albion is a Neoteny?

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:18.460
Seriously?

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:40.690
They did a good job cleaning it up, but someone definitely bled here.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:41.650
What?

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:46.450
But it isn't Lady Seiren's blood.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:58.880
It's me.

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:01.170
Where's the installation device?

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:03.380
It's been safely relocated.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.880
Then take it to the place I directed you to.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:11.100
Understood, Lord Robin.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:18.940
Where's Lady Seiren?

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:22.610
She wasn't on the second floor.

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:26.950
This just keeps getting more complicated.

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:33.490
Let's go, Amara.

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:34.910
Yeah.

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:55.020
The gentle breeze sweeps away even tears

00:22:55.020 --> 00:23:00.480
Even the recollections of the way of the stars

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:05.320
aren't always good things

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:12.990
I met you again on that faraway day

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:22.460
Even though we're as close as we are, this distant day is beginning

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:30.720
You can hear my voice calling out when I'm all alone

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:36.680
More than just love, it's hard to put into words

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:42.520
I'm searching for what to say while I walk beside you

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:45.610
Instead of saying goodbye,

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:53.780
I'll just put these love spun tears in my right pocket again tomorrow

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:57.200
Love is spreading across the world

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:03.330
And I finally found it, by your side

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:15.220
Every night, illegal fighting matches

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:18.810
are held at an underground ring in this town.

00:24:18.810 --> 00:24:22.020
Of course, bets are placed on the fights.

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:26.270
And the next Machine Goodfellow is going to appear in this town.

00:24:26.770 --> 00:24:31.150
Is the enemy one of the boys who are forced to fight?

00:24:31.150 --> 00:24:33.950
Next time, on episode 12 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:35.870
Boys' Battlefield.

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:35.870
Boys' Battlefield

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:38.580
Earth Engine, scramble!
